NOTICE
======

Provenance of the derived datasets
----------------------------------

Several CSV files in this repository are statistics computed from used-car
adverts published on bilbasen.dk, observed between June and September 2026 by
`depreciation/scrape_bilbasen.py`.

The underlying corpus of adverts is NOT distributed with this repository, and
should not be added to it. It is a database in which bilbasen.dk holds rights,
including the sui generis database right under Directive 96/9/EC (in Denmark,
ophavsretsloven § 71); extracting or re-utilising a substantial part of it is
reserved to the rightsholder. What is published here instead:

  * per-brand and per-fuel-type depreciation rates, mileage elasticities, and
    fitted comparator prices — statistics about the market, not a copy of it;

  * two small extracts kept as audit trails for specific case studies
    (`depreciation/solterra_bz4x_data.csv`, ~100 rows;
    `fuel-cost/comparator-listings.csv`, ~140 rows), with the columns that
    point at an individual advert or locate its seller removed, and
    private-seller rows dropped.

The CC BY 4.0 licence in LICENSE-CONTENT is granted over this project's own
selection, computation and presentation. It does not and cannot grant any right
in bilbasen.dk's underlying data. If you intend to reuse these figures at scale
or commercially, satisfy yourself independently on that point.

Prices, taxes and specifications
--------------------------------

Figures quoted from manufacturers, dealers, Skatteforvaltningen,
Motorstyrelsen, Forsyningstilsynet and public price comparison sites are
reproduced as factual data for analysis, with the retrieval date given at the
point of use. Trade marks and model names are the property of their respective
owners and are used descriptively.

One service tariff is sourced from a written quote issued by an authorised
Subaru workshop in Denmark on 3 September 2026. The workshop is not named and
the quote document is not reproduced: it was issued to an individual rather than
published as a tariff, and the document itself carries vehicle identifiers. Only
the two price figures it establishes are used.

No advice
---------

Nothing here is financial, tax or legal advice. The analyses are one person's
working notes about one purchase decision in Denmark in 2026, with their
assumptions stated so that a reader can disagree with them. Several of the most
load-bearing numbers are explicitly labelled as estimates in the notes
themselves. Check anything you intend to rely on.

